ty_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the concrete live seam that sequences a provider create before a dependent create and holds the dependent on the provider's CoordinatedCreateOutcome (e.g. route creates through the coordinator's dependency order, or add a per-pass create-ordering pass that consults should_hold_dependent), since reroute_migrated_plans excludes creates and should_hold_dependent currently has no production caller.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["batch_dispatch.py:591-599 reroute_migrated_plans filters to `m.action.value in NON_CREATE_FAMILIES` — creates are never routed through the coordinator","batch_dispatch.py:244 NON_CREATE_FAMILIES excludes 'create'","create_route.py:210 should_hold_dependent has zero production callers (only tests reference it)","requires_parent/requires_create are consumed only by ticket_planner (shadow) and tests — no live create-loop consumer","Plan: 'Wire CREATE plans through the existing create-specific coordination/dispatch seam' names a seam that coordinates a single create, not inter-create ordering"],"finding":"The plan asserts the LIVE create route sequences the provider create ahead of a dependent and holds the dependent on the provider's outcome, but no such cross-create ordering seam exists in the live path: reroute_migrated_plans excludes creates (NON_CREATE_FAMILIES), creates dispatch per-mutation through legacy handle_create/create_one, and should_hold_dependent has no production caller. coordinate_full_create governs a single create plan, not the ordering of one create relative to a dependent create.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd24cf84bead27744","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / AC5 / AC6","norm_id":"n67796d254089e25a","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Parent and child both unbound in one pass: the legacy create loop dispatches them in batch order with no guarantee the parent is created/bound before the child, and no mechanism defers the child on the parent's CoordinatedCreateOutcome"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"high","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"hard","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"no_executable_breakdown","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Pin the storage representation of requires_create/requires_parent (dedicated OutboundCreatePayload attributes vs. entries in fields) and make the from_legacy/as_legacy_dict round trip and the _mutation_to_batch_dict strip consistent with that single choice.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["mutation_payloads.py:120-137 from_legacy spreads every unrecognized key into `fields` — so a prerequisite key stored as a plain mapping entry lands in fields","batch_dispatch.py:145-151 create branch does `fields = dict(mutation.payload.fields)` — only strips what is in fields","Plan says both 'carry them as explicit metadata on OutboundMutation' and '_mutation_to_batch_dict must strip scheduler metadata from vendor fields' without pinning the storage location"],"finding":"The plan is ambiguous about whether the prerequisite local IDs are stored inside payload.fields (the vendor spread, which then genuinely needs stripping in _mutation_to_batch_dict) or as dedicated OutboundCreatePayload attributes (in which case from_legacy would not spread them into fields and the create branch's `dict(payload.fields)` never leaks them). The AC4 strip requirement and the round-trip contract depend on which representation is chosen.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7097afda731c8c4e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / AC2 / AC4 / Scope (mutation_payloads.py)","norm_id":"nc8265914235e8a5f","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If prerequisites are dedicated attributes, the AC4 strip is a no-op and the planner-visible top-level mapping requirement (AC2) must be satisfied via _PayloadMapping.get, not the fields spread"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how a released child create obtains its parent reference after the provider binds (e.g. re-derive the parent field from the now-bound parent at dispatch time, or defer the child to the next pass where the parent field re-materializes) so parent-before-child ordering actually yields a linked child rather than a parentless create.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["outbound_mutation_builders.py:122-134: `suppressed_parents` collects the parent field and drops it (dropped_field_sink) when the parent is unbound at emission time","Plan forbids a local-ID↔Jira-key conversion layer, yet the vendor create ultimately needs the parent's real Jira key to set the parent field","Prior-round note in review cache: 'State how the child create's parent field is populated within the same pass after the parent create persists its local-ID→Jira mapping'"],"finding":"Even with correct parent-before-child ordering, the plan never states how the child create acquires its parent link. The builder suppresses the parent field whenever the parent is unbound (suppressed_parents), and the plan explicitly forbids any local-ID↔Jira-key conversion layer, so the held child would still be emitted without a parent reference — making the ordering observationally inert (it solves a proxy: 'run parent first' without achieving 'child is linked to parent').","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,